  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lifts the no-duplicate-per-(application,eventType) constraint; injecting two indistinguishable audit entries for the same application+event forces a counterexample within the Alloy scope, which both append-only assertions must detect.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets Alloy invent an Operation whose (role, kind) is not in the permission matrix; the injection forces a customer-issued PostDecision, which is a denied cell, so both the catalogue LeastPrivilege check and the staff-only-decision FR must fail.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_015_StaffOnlyDecision
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_StaffOnlyDecision: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets an application exist without a Submitted audit entry; injection forces such an application into existence within scope, so both the per-application Submitted-event check and the audit-completeness pattern must fail.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_016_AuditAppendOnly
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedAccess  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedAccess.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lifts the customer/own-resource gate on GetApplicationById; the injection constructs an Operation where a customer successfully sees another customer's application, which is exactly the leak FR-013 and the two patterns must catch.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, NoInformationLeakage, FR_013_CustomerOwnAccess
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_CustomerOwnAccess: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequired  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AuthRequired.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets an unauthenticated Operation reach a handler; the injection forces existence of an op with authenticated=False, which both auth-required assertions must reject.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OnePendingPerCustomer  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OnePendingPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets one customer hold two simultaneous Pending Review applications; the injection makes two such applications co-exist for the same customer, which violates the partial unique index and so the FR-005 assertion.
    expected to FAIL: FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer
      - FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

